<title>USA: Bell Atlantic files with FCC against AT&amp;T.</title>
<headline>Bell Atlantic files with FCC against AT&amp;T.</headline>
<dateline>ARLINGTON, Va. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bell Atlantic Corp said Monday it has filed a protest with the U.S. Federal Communications Commission, alleging AT&amp;T Corp has pocketed hundreds of millions of dollars in access charge savings rather than passing them along to customers.</p>
<p>The regional Bell company accused AT&amp;T of backing out of a promise it made previously to pass on to its long distance customers the savings from cuts the FCC ordered in the access fees long distance companies pay local phone service providers such as Bell Atlantic.</p>
</text>
